\
The living spirit grows and even outgrows its earlier forms.  It chooses the men [sic] who proclaim it and in whom it lives.  This living spirit is eternally renewed and pursues its goal in manifold and inconceivable ways throughout the history of mankind.  Measured against it, the names and forms which men have given it mean very little; they are only the changing leaves and blossoms on the stem of the eternal tree.\
\pard\li270\fi-270\qr
\cf2 	C. G. Jung 
